  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1142 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nLong range global models are showing the development of a tropical \nsystem in the Gulf and a developing trough taking shape over the \nwestern CONUS. The GFS wants to keep this trough more compact while \nthe ECMWF wants to evolve the trough into a much deeper low over the \nGreat Basin thus promoting a southwesterly flow aloft impinging on \nthe southern plains. The GFS solution is showing a much stronger \nzonal flow across our area as the trough moves east in response to \nthe next shortwave trough entering the west coast. Since this is \nstill a week away confidence is low in regards to choosing any \nparticular solution at this time. However these systems evolve this \ntrough will likely bring the next chance of rain into the southern \nplains.",
